{
  "#comment": [
    "Canonical overall length in METERS for each TNG hull, and the scale convention",
    "the roster is held to.",
    "",
    "UNITS_PER_METER is not invented here. It was MEASURED off the shipped meshes:",
    "bounding box of media/ships/<root>.obj times that hull's meshscale is the size the",
    "engine actually draws, and 14 of the 36 checkable hulls already land within 1% of",
    "0.400 u/m. So this is the convention the pack already holds, written down - not a",
    "new one imposed on it.",
    "",
    "'source' says how much weight a figure carries:",
    "  onscreen  - an official figure (Memory Alpha / a Tech Manual / an okudagram).",
    "              Treat as fixed.",
    "  approx    - licensed or fan-consensus, no official number exists. Fine to adjust,",
    "              but adjust it HERE so the checker and the ship data cannot disagree.",
    "  by_class  - deliberately absent. An original or STO design with no length to",
    "              check against, or a station whose true size would dwarf the play",
    "              area. scale_report skips these; they are sized from their weight",
    "              class instead. Do NOT invent a number to fill one of these in."
  ],
  "units_per_meter": 0.4,
  "tolerance": {
    "scale_lo": 0.38,
    "scale_hi": 0.42,
    "excl_lo": 0.45,
    "excl_hi": 0.6
  },
  "exclusion_ratio": 0.52,
